 "texts": {
  "description": "In the Arena, Invoker and Titan Stats are modified to ensure fast Battles, more Titans, and better balance.",
  "effects-scaling-title": "Certain buffs and debuffs will have their durations modified, based on the Skill they are applied by and the number of targets they affect.",
  "diminishing-title": "Whenever someone receives a Control debuff, a 10-second timer starts: the Diminishing Durations Window. Subsequent Control debuffs placed within this 10-second window will have Diminished Durations.",
  "diminishing-mid": "The timer starts as soon as the Control debuff is placed",
  "diminishing-first": "The next Control debuff placed within the 10-second window will have a diminished duration",
  "diminishing-last": "The target is now effectively immune to Control debuffs for 7 seconds once the last active Control debuff expires",
  "diminishing-example": "Example: The first Control debuff placed was a 10 second Stun. During those 10 seconds, 4 more Control debuffs were placed on the target, each for 5 seconds. The 7-second immunity window only begins once the initial 10-second Stun debuff expires.",
  "titan-bound-effet": "Bound Effects work as normal."
 },
 "unconfirmed": [
  "healthBonus (8): read as Invoker HP x8 in Arena; the config gives the number only.",
  "titanStatsMultiplier (0.05): what the Titan's stats are multiplied by in Arena (as named in the config).",
  "initialCooldownFactor is 0.5 in config, so skills would start with cooldowns 50% done (or 50% remaining). The in-battle PvP tip says 70%; the tip may be outdated.",
  "effectDurationPercent: percent of the normal duration a buff/debuff lasts in Arena, by the kind of skill that applied it (single-target or AOE)."
 ]
